Follow sfall's speed, middle mouse button and item highlights in ddraw.ini

What else Fallout Fixt sets in its ddraw.ini (see the patch before):

- [Speed] Enable and SpeedMultiInitial: the game runs that much faster (Fixt:
  110%) on the map, in combat and on the world map, as sfall does - not in the
  screens and menus. The game's clock goes faster while their loops wait for
  input; it never jumps when it goes on or off.
- [Input] MiddleMouse: the middle mouse button presses that key (Fixt: B, which
  switches hands).
- [Input] ToggleItemHighlightsKey and TurnHighlightContainers: while that key
  is held (Fixt: left Shift), items on the ground are outlined in yellow, and
  containers and the bodies that can be searched in grey; an item keeps its
  outline once the cursor leaves it. The page can hold the key down for a touch
  screen, as for Fallout 2.

Keys are DirectInput scan codes, as sfall reads them.
